<title>SPAIN: Banesto cuts prime rate to 7.25 pct.</title>
<headline>Banesto cuts prime rate to 7.25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bank Banco Espanol de Credito lowered its prime rate to 7.25 percent from 7.50 percent effective on Friday.</p>
<p>The move follows the Bank of Spain's decision earlier to cut its key money market rate to 5.75 percent from 6.00 percent.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
